  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Papillon (French Fishing). Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Papillon (Butterfly) is a classic French fishing-type card game, conceptually similar to Scopa but with its own distinct bonus system and 'Talon' (stock) mechanics. Players use cards from their hand to capture cards from the table, either by matching ranks or sums. It is beloved for its evocative bonus names ('Grasshopper', 'Little Beetle') and its emphasis on being the first to 'fly away' by emptying one's hand. It is primarily a game of observation and tactical capturing.",
    objective: 'Score points by capturing cards and clearing the table; be the first to empty your hand after the talon is exhausted (papillon) to sweep the pool.',
    gameplay: 'Players in turn play one card to capture: a table card of the same rank, or a set of table cards whose total equals the played card, or three of a rank from hand to capture the fourth from the table. Captured cards form a trick placed face down. If unable to capture (e.g. after a sauterelle sweep), the player trails all hand cards face up to the tableau. When all hands are empty, the dealer gives 3 more cards each from the talon. When the talon is exhausted, the first to empty their hand by taking a trick wins the deal (papillon) and sweeps the pool.',
    keyRules: [
      'Capture by same rank, by sum (played card equals total of table cards), or three-of-a-rank to take the fourth from table.',
      'If you cannot capture, you must trail (play all hand cards face up to the tableau).',
      'Sauterelle: sweeping all table cards forces the next player to trail.',
      'Winner of the deal is first to empty hand by taking a trick after talon is exhausted; tie-break: dealer, second hand, first hand.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '3 is the traditional count.',
      deck: '52 cards. Each player receives 3 cards initially; 7 more face-up to the tableau (3 players) or 4 (4 players); remainder as talon. After each round when hands are empty, deal 3 more each from talon.',
      equipment: 'Counters (jetons, fiches) for scoring.',
      dealing: "Deal 3 cards each to hand (first hand to dealer's left), then 7 face-up to the tableau (4 in four-hand). Stack the remainder face down as talon. When all hands are empty, deal 3 more each from talon.",
    },
    turnFlow: 'Players in turn play one card to capture: a table card of the same rank, or a set of table cards whose total equals the played card, or three of a rank from hand to capture the fourth from the table. Captured cards form a trick placed face down. If unable to capture (e.g. after a sauterelle sweep), the player trails all hand cards face up to the tableau. When all hands are empty, the dealer gives 3 more cards each from the talon. When the talon is exhausted, the first to empty their hand by taking a trick wins the deal (papillon) and sweeps the pool.',
